WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.769
-Our first guest tonight
is a talented actor

00:00:02.769 --> 00:00:04.837
who you know from his work
as Peter Parker

00:00:04.837 --> 00:00:06.272
from both
the "Spider-Man" movies

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:07.707
and the "Avengers" franchise.

00:00:07.707 --> 00:00:10.977
His latest film, "Uncharted,"
is in theaters and IMAX now.

00:00:10.977 --> 00:00:12.645
Let's take a look.

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:14.046
-Do you think
it's another puzzle?

00:00:14.046 --> 00:00:15.849
-Well, whatever it is,
you better figure it out fast.

00:00:15.849 --> 00:00:18.885
I'm gonna try
and buy us some time.

00:00:18.885 --> 00:00:20.352
Hey, can I get you a drink?

00:00:20.352 --> 00:00:21.988
-Gin and tonic, por favor.

00:00:21.988 --> 00:00:24.357
-This definitely isn't a gin and
tonic, but it is on the house.

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:26.525
-Gracias.

00:00:26.525 --> 00:00:30.529
-Hey, whoa, whoa, whoa.
Let me guess, piña colada?

00:00:30.529 --> 00:00:32.531
[ Crowd gasps ]

00:00:32.531 --> 00:00:34.334
-[ Grunting ]
[ Crowd gasps ]

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:35.568
-The eye.

00:00:35.568 --> 00:00:37.970
-[ Grunting ]

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:39.939
-Think you're a comedian there,
sunshine.

00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:41.507
-Okay, I got it, I got it.

00:00:41.507 --> 00:00:42.909
Sex on the Beach.

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:44.510
-Please welcome back to the show

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:46.412
our friend Tom Holland,
everybody.

00:00:46.412 --> 00:00:48.448
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:48.448 --> 00:00:57.857 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:57.857 --> 00:01:07.233 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:09.436
Welcome back, my friend.

00:01:09.436 --> 00:01:10.770
-Hello, mate.
It's good to be back.

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:12.505
-It's great to have you here.

00:01:12.505 --> 00:01:13.973
Last time you were here --

00:01:13.973 --> 00:01:16.175
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:16.175 --> 00:01:17.910
-Oh.
-This is very appropriate

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:19.579
because, you know,
last time you were here,

00:01:19.579 --> 00:01:22.281
you were promoting
the new "Spider-Man" film.

00:01:22.281 --> 00:01:23.416
-Yes, I was, yeah.

00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:25.484
-And it's done quite well
for itself.

00:01:25.484 --> 00:01:27.353
-Yeah, the studio were happy.

00:01:27.353 --> 00:01:28.854
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:28.854 --> 00:01:30.122
It's interesting,
with your show,

00:01:30.122 --> 00:01:31.891
I feel like you can do a, like,

00:01:31.891 --> 00:01:33.826
through the ages
of me growing up.

00:01:33.826 --> 00:01:36.195
I came here, I don't know,
I was maybe 19.

00:01:36.195 --> 00:01:37.963
I'm 25 now.
-Yep.

00:01:37.963 --> 00:01:39.532
-It's always great
to be back here, mate.

00:01:39.532 --> 00:01:40.633
So thanks for having me back.

00:01:40.633 --> 00:01:42.968
-And every time you come,
I say to you --

00:01:42.968 --> 00:01:44.270
I'm like, "I don't think
it's going to work.

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:46.439
I don't think show biz
is going to work for you."

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:48.240
And you keep ignoring me,
and I'm so happy.

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:51.444
-Yeah, constantly
[bleep] myself.

00:01:51.444 --> 00:01:55.080
-But a tremendous -- I mean,
a movie that is so deserved.

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:58.017
And one thing, of course,
every time you're here,

00:01:58.017 --> 00:02:00.753
especially if it's for anything
Marvel, one of the problems is,

00:02:00.753 --> 00:02:03.256
you have to promote a film that
you can say very little about.

00:02:03.256 --> 00:02:06.292
-Very true, very true, yeah.

00:02:06.292 --> 00:02:09.262
I am a very honest person
just by nature.

00:02:09.262 --> 00:02:11.164
-Yeah.

00:02:11.164 --> 00:02:13.266
-Which has got me into trouble
in the past.

00:02:13.266 --> 00:02:16.235
-Yeah. It seems like
you're even nervous now

00:02:16.235 --> 00:02:17.870
you're going to spoil a movie
that everyone has seen.

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:19.906
-That is already out there.
-Yeah.

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:21.574
-But every time I say, like,
"So Tobey --"

00:02:21.574 --> 00:02:24.176
I'm like, "Shh, shut up,
don't say that."

00:02:24.176 --> 00:02:25.545
But yeah, I'm just very honest.

00:02:25.545 --> 00:02:27.947
So on the press tour, you know,
journalists are like,

00:02:27.947 --> 00:02:29.615
"So were Tobey and Andrew
in this movie?"

00:02:29.615 --> 00:02:31.550
I'm like, "No, they're not.
Stop asking me that."

00:02:31.550 --> 00:02:33.719
And I go home
and I almost can't sleep

00:02:33.719 --> 00:02:35.922
because I feel so bad
for lying all the time.

00:02:35.922 --> 00:02:38.023
-Yeah.
-I'm, like, calling up my mom.

00:02:38.023 --> 00:02:40.727
I'm like, "I just feel so guilty
for all the lies."

00:02:40.727 --> 00:02:42.095
[ Laughter ]

00:02:42.095 --> 00:02:43.563
-Have you -- You should just go,

00:02:43.563 --> 00:02:44.931
you should call
all those journalists

00:02:44.931 --> 00:02:46.932
and be like, "I'm so sorry."
-I know, yeah.

00:02:46.932 --> 00:02:49.301
-"I feel terrible about it.
I hope you understand."

00:02:49.301 --> 00:02:50.703
-Yeah, I don't feel that sorry,
though.

00:02:50.703 --> 00:02:52.204
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.204 --> 00:02:55.475
What was -- I mean, that is the
spoiler that could not be said

00:02:55.475 --> 00:02:57.209
that we can now
let the world know.

00:02:57.209 --> 00:02:59.712
But what was it like to work
with Andrew and Tobey,

00:02:59.712 --> 00:03:01.814
the previous Spider-Men?

00:03:01.814 --> 00:03:04.650
-Honestly, mate, it was

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:07.086
the most incredible experience
of my career.

00:03:07.086 --> 00:03:08.354
To share the screen with them --

00:03:08.354 --> 00:03:09.788
You know, playing Spider-Man,

00:03:09.788 --> 00:03:12.959
while being
a wonderful experience

00:03:12.959 --> 00:03:14.961
and, like, completely
life-changing,

00:03:14.961 --> 00:03:16.762
it also can be quite alienating.

00:03:16.762 --> 00:03:17.830
You know, when you're 19

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:19.398
and someone gives you
this opportunity

00:03:19.398 --> 00:03:21.034
and your life changes,

00:03:21.034 --> 00:03:23.736
it's quite hard to figure out
how to navigate.

00:03:23.736 --> 00:03:26.071
So to almost have
like two older brothers

00:03:26.071 --> 00:03:28.074
that had been through it
before me,

00:03:28.074 --> 00:03:30.309
to be able to share
that experience with them

00:03:30.309 --> 00:03:31.744
was amazing.

00:03:31.744 --> 00:03:33.946
And I remember we were
shooting this scene,

00:03:33.946 --> 00:03:35.080
which was really emotional --

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:37.083
like, a really,
really emotional scene,

00:03:37.083 --> 00:03:40.052
and I was struggling to find the
emotion just because, you know,

00:03:40.052 --> 00:03:41.086
when you make these big movies,

00:03:41.086 --> 00:03:42.655
it can take two days
to shoot a scene.

00:03:42.655 --> 00:03:44.957
I'd been crying for days on end.

00:03:44.957 --> 00:03:47.393
So I went up to Andrew
and Tobey --

00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:48.961
I nearly said Spider-Man
and Spider-Man.

00:03:48.961 --> 00:03:50.829
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.829 --> 00:03:53.165
And I basically just said,

00:03:53.165 --> 00:03:54.934
"Thank you,
thank you for being here.

00:03:54.934 --> 00:03:56.869
Thank you for taking the time

00:03:56.869 --> 00:03:59.638
to be a part of this, you know,
incredible opportunity.

00:03:59.638 --> 00:04:00.873
It means the world to me."

00:04:00.873 --> 00:04:03.776
And we all embraced,
and we all started crying.

00:04:03.776 --> 00:04:05.945
And I remember the writers
sort of seeing that,

00:04:05.945 --> 00:04:08.815
being like, "Yep, that's how
we're going to end the film.

00:04:08.815 --> 00:04:09.849
[ Laughter ]

00:04:09.849 --> 00:04:11.751
That's brilliant.
Well done, Tom."

00:04:11.751 --> 00:04:13.786
And then the end of the film
is us having this moment

00:04:13.786 --> 00:04:15.020
where I'm like,
"Thank you so much.

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:16.322
I really appreciate it."

00:04:16.322 --> 00:04:18.558
And then we have this
beautiful hug, so it was's nice.

00:04:18.558 --> 00:04:19.826
-That's really great
that you can both talk about

00:04:19.826 --> 00:04:21.627
the experience
of playing Spider-Man,

00:04:21.627 --> 00:04:23.095
which is obviously unique
to you guys,

00:04:23.095 --> 00:04:24.797
and also wearing
the Spider-Man suit.

00:04:24.797 --> 00:04:27.566
Because not a lot of people,
you know, do it at that level.

00:04:27.566 --> 00:04:29.001
It's just, like,
the three of you

00:04:29.001 --> 00:04:30.102
and that guy in Times Square.

00:04:30.102 --> 00:04:31.270
-I'll give you a spoiler.

00:04:31.270 --> 00:04:33.439
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-You don't want to hug him.

00:04:33.439 --> 00:04:35.174
Do not hug him.
-I'll give you a spoiler,

00:04:35.174 --> 00:04:37.009
and I'm not going to
tell you who,

00:04:37.009 --> 00:04:39.312
but one of us has a fake ass
in their suit.

00:04:39.312 --> 00:04:41.647
-Really?
[ Laughter ]

00:04:41.647 --> 00:04:43.082
Wow.

00:04:43.082 --> 00:04:44.817
-You can figure out that
for yourselves.

00:04:44.817 --> 00:04:46.118
-Well.

00:04:46.118 --> 00:04:48.621
I mean, see, this is a real --
This is, you know --

00:04:48.621 --> 00:04:50.289
Everybody thinks you're
such a nice guy,

00:04:50.289 --> 00:04:51.958
but you're all about
ticket sales.

00:04:51.958 --> 00:04:55.328
Because now everybody
is going back out

00:04:55.328 --> 00:04:56.896
to try to find the fake ass.

00:04:56.896 --> 00:04:58.597
-I remember being on set
and being like,

00:04:58.597 --> 00:05:01.200
"Wow!
Oh, hang on a minute.

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:03.402
No, that's not real."
-Right?

00:05:03.402 --> 00:05:05.871
At the wrap party, you're like,
"Where'd his ass go?"

00:05:05.871 --> 00:05:08.307
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:08.307 --> 00:05:11.944
-This is -- This is very fun,
to do a film like this.

00:05:11.944 --> 00:05:14.913
And I want to mention the clip
real quick.

00:05:14.913 --> 00:05:17.849
You actually looked like
you had some bartending skills.

00:05:17.849 --> 00:05:19.385
And I asked about it,

00:05:19.385 --> 00:05:20.787
and you actually did
take this seriously.

00:05:20.787 --> 00:05:23.022
You did a little bit
of bartending classes.

00:05:23.022 --> 00:05:24.824
-Yeah, it was
an interesting one.

00:05:24.824 --> 00:05:26.459
Nathan Drake as a character

00:05:26.459 --> 00:05:29.828
is someone
who is incredibly capable

00:05:29.828 --> 00:05:32.431
but in no way, shape,
or form trained.

00:05:32.431 --> 00:05:34.967
So I wanted to find something

00:05:34.967 --> 00:05:37.803
where I could convince
the audiences of his skill,

00:05:37.803 --> 00:05:40.239
and I'd seen on YouTube
this flair bartending,

00:05:40.239 --> 00:05:41.507
and I thought it was always
really cool.

00:05:41.507 --> 00:05:42.875
So I thought that would be
a great way

00:05:42.875 --> 00:05:45.144
to demonstrate to the audiences
that he's quite handy.

00:05:45.144 --> 00:05:47.813
So I started taking
bartending classes,

00:05:47.813 --> 00:05:51.016
and I actually went
to my favorite bar in London

00:05:51.016 --> 00:05:52.819
and managed to convince
the bartenders

00:05:52.819 --> 00:05:54.620
to let me go behind the bar.

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:57.389
So I ended up working these
kind of undercover shifts.

00:05:57.389 --> 00:05:59.726
I had, like, the white tuxedo on
and everything.

00:05:59.726 --> 00:06:01.660
-Yeah.
-But then the management team

00:06:01.660 --> 00:06:05.130
found out, and I haven't
been allowed back since.

00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:06.698
-In what -- in what --

00:06:06.698 --> 00:06:09.334
I was going to say when
you had to convince them,

00:06:09.334 --> 00:06:12.605
like, in what world do people
say, "No, Tom Holland.

00:06:12.605 --> 00:06:15.641
You don't have your
bartender's license."

00:06:15.641 --> 00:06:17.643
-I think the big part of it
was that, like,

00:06:17.643 --> 00:06:20.212
they're charging a lot of money
and my drinks taste like [bleep]

00:06:20.212 --> 00:06:22.315
-Oh, I see.
-And the patrons weren't happy.

00:06:22.315 --> 00:06:23.783
-Yeah, like on Yelp,
they were like,

00:06:23.783 --> 00:06:28.354
"While the espresso martini
was made by Tom Holland,

00:06:28.354 --> 00:06:30.589
it tasted like [bleep]"

00:06:30.589 --> 00:06:32.157
Three stars.
-Yeah, exactly.

00:06:32.157 --> 00:06:33.959
-I have more questions
about "Uncharted."

00:06:33.959 --> 00:06:36.062
We'll be right back with more
from Tom Holland.

